{
  "_comment": [
    "Name rules for scripts/size-report.js. Each top-level statement of the IIFE goes to the FIRST subsystem (in this order) one of whose `names` patterns matches a name the statement declares (function, const/let, call or assignment target) and none of whose `exclude` patterns does. Unmatched statements go to `fallback`.",
    "Names, not line numbers: the same rules classify older revisions (--rev). Prefix traps from org/build-framework.org 2026-10-10: _sleepInterruptible is not springsteenlyrics, _bbPrev/_bbH3/_bbStep/_bbIcon are MusicBrainz 'bigbox' locals, not Brucebase.",
    "memberSplits: members of a big literal that belong elsewhere. configSchema keys by key name; pageDefinitions entries by 'host:' + type when the entry has a host property (a foreign-site pageType)."
  ],
  "fallback": "engine",
  "fallbackLabel": "Engine: fetch, DOM pre-processing, filter, sort, render, init (rest)",
  "subsystems": [
    { "id": "testhook", "label": "Test-mode hook (__saTest)", "names": ["^__saTest$", "^_saTest"] },
